              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To log into Microsoft OneDrive, use the official links and instructions below depending on how you want to access your files:\n\n### 1. Web Browser (Direct Login)\nIf you want to access your files right away using a web browser:\n* Go directly to the **[Microsoft OneDrive Sign-In Page](https://onedrive.live.com/)**.\n* Enter your Microsoft account email address (such as Outlook, Hotmail, Live, or a school/work email address) and click **Next**.\n* Enter your password and click **Sign in**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Windows Desktop App\nOneDrive is built into Windows 10 and Windows 11. To log in:\n1. Click the **Start menu** or press the **Windows key**.\n2. Type **OneDrive** and press **Enter** to open the app.\n3. If you aren't signed in, a setup window will appear. Enter your Microsoft email address and click **Sign in**.\n4. Enter your password and follow the on-screen prompts to choose your folder sync options.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Mac App\n1. Open the **App Store** on your Mac and download/install **Microsoft OneDrive** (if you haven't already).\n2. Open **OneDrive** from your Applications folder or Launchpad.\n3. Enter your Microsoft account credentials and follow the instructions to sync your files to your Mac.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Mobile App (iOS / Android)\n1. Download the **Microsoft OneDrive** app from the App Store (iOS) or Google Play Store (Android).\n2. Open the app and tap **Sign in**.\n3. Enter your Microsoft account email and password to access your files and back up your phone\u2019s photos.",
